1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giuliano_de%27_Medici
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Giuliano de' Medici''' (1453 – April 26, 1478) was the second son of Piero de' Medici (the Gouty). As co-ruler of Florence, with his brother Lorenzo the Magnificent, he complemented his brother's image as the "patron of the art
2 CONC s" with his own image as the handsome "sporting golden boy."
2 CONT
2 CONT As the opening stroke of the Pazzi Conspiracy, he was assassinated in the Duomo of Florence, Santa Maria del Fiore, by Francesco de' Pazzi and Bernardo Bandini. He was stabbed 19 times and was said to have died instantly.
2 CONT
2 CONT Giulio di Giuliano de' Medici, Giuliano's illegitimate son by his mistress Fioretta Gorini, went on to become Pope Clement VII.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is buried with his brother Lorenzo in the Medici Chapel of the Church of San Lorenzo; their tomb is ornamented with the Madonna and Child of Michelangelo."
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
2 CONT *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORTHERN%20ITALY%20after%201400.htm#PieroMedicideid1469B
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         '''GIULIANO de' Medici''' (Florence 25 Oct 1453-murdered Florence 26 Apr 1478).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mistress''' (1):  FIORETTA Gorini, daughter of ANTONIO Gorini & his wife --- (-1478).  
2 CONT
2 CONT   Giuliano had one illegitimate child by Mistress (1): 
2 CONT *a)         GIOVANNI GIULIO de' Medici (Florence 6 Mar or 26 May 1478-Rome 25 Sep 1534).  He was elected Pope Clement VII in 1523. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
