1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://documents.medici.org/ Online Archive of Medici Family Documents]
2 CONT * Wikipedia: [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carlo_de%27_Medici_%281430%E2%80%931492%29 Carlo de' Medici (1430–1492)]
2 CONT
2 CONT Carlo di Cosimo de 'Medici (Florence, 1428 or 1430 - Florence, May 29, 1492) was an Italian Priest. He was the illegitimate son of Cosimo de' Medici (the Elder) and a slave Circassian named Magdalene. His father forced him to take
2 CONC  on a religious life.
2 CONT
2 CONT After becoming Canon of the cathedral at Florence in 1450, he was appointed rector of Pieve di Santa Maria (Dicomano) in Mugello and San Donato di Calenzano. He became Abbot of San Salvatore in Vaiano. He was also responsible for 
2 CONC making the main drain and Nuncio in Tuscany. He was already dean of Prato in 1460.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on May 29, 1492.
