2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giovanni_di_Bicci_de%27_Medici
2 CONT
2 CONT Giovanni di Bicci de' Medici (c. 1360 – February 20/28, 1429) was an Italian banker, a member of Medici family of Florence, and the founder of the Medici Bank. While other family members, such as Chiarissimo di Giambuono de' Medic
2 CONC i, who served in the Signoria in 1201, and Salvestro de' Medici, who was implicated in the Ciompi Revolt of 1378, are historically significant, Giovanni's founding of the family bank truly began the family's rise to power in Flore
2 CONC nce. He was the father of Cosimo de' Medici (Pater Patriae), grandfather of Piero di Cosimo de' Medici, great-grandfather of Lorenzo de' Medici (the Magnificent) and great-great-great-grandfather of Cosimo I de' Medici, Grand Duke
2 CONC  of Tuscany.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORTHERN%20ITALY%20after%201400.htm#GiacomoAveradoMedicidied1429B
2 CONT
2 CONT GIOVANNI “di Bicci” de' Medici, son of AVERADO [III] de´ Medici & his [second wife Giacoma Spini] (1360-Florence 20 Feb 1429).  Elected “Prior” of the guild of bankers 1402, 1408 and 1411.  Podestà di Pistoia 1407.  Elected Gonfal
2 CONC ionere di Giustizia of the Republic of Florence 1421. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' PICCARDA de' Bueri, daughter of ODOARDO de' Bueri & his wife --- (-1432). 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Giovanni & his wife had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
