1 OCCU si dedicò in gioventù agli affari economici di famiglia, acquisendo una grandissima a solida ricchezza, per poi dedicarsi alla vita politica cittadina
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} - http://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/jacopo-salviati_(Dizionario-Biografico)/
2 CONT
2 CONT - https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacopo_Salviati
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Giovanni Salviati and Maddalena Gondi, he devoted himself in the economic affairs of the family, becoming very wealthy. He then engaged in political life. He was married to the prestigious Lucrezia de' Medici, daughter of L
2 CONC orenzo de' Medici, on September 10 1486.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Prior of the Guilds (see Guilds of Florence) in 1499 and 1518, then gonfalonier of Justice in 1514. In 1513, he was appointed ambassador to Rome.
2 CONT
2 CONT He tried to prevent the Siege of Florence (1529–1530), but without result, and was among the advisers of Pope Clement VII during his meeting with Charles V, Holy Roman Emperor.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1531, he was part of the balìa of 200 Florentine citizens charged with reforming the republican government.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 6 September 1533.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Children
2 CONT
2 CONT His marriage to Lucrezia produced ten children,
2 CONT
2 CONT Cardinal Giovanni Salviati (Florence, 1490 - Ravenna, 1553)
2 CONT
2 CONT Lorenzo Salviati (Florence, 1492 - Ferrara, 1539), senator and patron
2 CONT
2 CONT Piero Salviati, patrician
2 CONT
2 CONT Elena Salviati (Florence, 1495 circa - Genoa, 1552), married the Marquis Pallavicino Pallavicino and second marriage to the Prince Jacopo V of Aragon in Appiano
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptist Salviati (1498 - 1524)
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Salviati (1499 - 1543), married to Giovanni dalle Bande Nere. This marriage reunited the main and Popolano branches of the Medici family. His son, Cosimo, was named to lead Florence after the death of Duke Alessandro de' Med
2 CONC ici
2 CONT
2 CONT Luisa Salviati, married Sigismund de Luna and Peralta
2 CONT
2 CONT Francesca Salviati, married first to Piero Gualterotti and second, in 1533, to Ottaviano de' Medici and was the mother of Pope Leo XI
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernardo Salviati (1505/1508 - Rome, 1568), was a knight of the Order of St. John of Jerusalem, created a Cardinal in 1561
2 CONT
2 CONT Alamanno (1510 - 1571), patrician
2 CONT
2 CONT These children all held great positions in Europe or were parents of important people.
