1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Alfonsina Orsini''' (1472 – 7 February 1520) was a Regent of Florence. She was the spouse of Piero di Lorenzo de' Medici from 1488 and the mother of Lorenzo II de' Medici. She was the daughter of Roberto Orsini,
2 CONC  Conte Tagliacozzo and Catherine San Severino.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is credited with a great influence over the affairs of state. She governed The Republic of Florence during the absence of her son in the period of 1515-1519. She was involved in the plans regarding the war between Florence and
2 CONC  France, as well as in the plans of making a treaty. She also had oversight of Pope Leo's entry into Florence in November 1515.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfonsina Orsini's maid, Simonetta da Collevecchio, was to-be the mother of Alessandro de' Medici.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfonsina_Orsini
2 CONT ------
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/G8QG-J68
