1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacopo_de%27_Pazzi
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jacopo de' Pazzi''' (1423 - 26 April 1478) became head of the Pazzi in 1464. He, his nephew Francesco, and his brother Renato were executed after the Pazzi conspiracy on 26 April 1478.
2 CONT
2 CONT The conspiracy was proposed in Montughi, at Jacopo Pazzi's villa, and it was planned to kill Lorenzo and Giuliano de' Medici and take over the government of Florence. After the conspiracy, Jacopo went home and he found Francesco w
2 CONC ith a wound in one leg, possibly self-inflicted. With 100 armed men, Jacopo ran through the streets crying "Liberty!", but when Francesco was dragged from his bed and hanged, Jacopo escaped from Florence. In the village of Castagn
2 CONC o he was recognised and sent back to Florence, where he was tortured and hanged next to the decomposing body of Francesco Salviati. After being buried at Santa Croce, his body was dug up, thrown in a ditch, dragged through the str
2 CONC eets, and propped up at the door of the Palazzo Pazzi, where his head was mockingly used as a door knocker. After that, his body was thrown into the Arno, where it was retrieved by children, hung from a willow tree, flogged, and t
2 CONC hrown back into the river.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stefano di Ser Niccolo da Bagnone served as a secretary to Jacopo and tutor to his daughter Caterina. Palazzo Pazzi was commissioned by Jacopo between 1462 and 1472.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
