1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/gino-capponi_res-d82ade3d-87e9-11dc-8e9d-0016357eee51_(Dizionario-Biografico)/
2 CONT
2 CONT CAPONI, Gino
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born on January 22, 1423 to Neri di Gino, and Selvaggia di Tommaso Sacchetti; the only surviving son, he was the only heir of his father, the most important political figure in Florence after Cosimo de' Medici. However, C. 
2 CONC did not have the same interest as his father in political life and preferred to devote his main activity to increasing the family's business and land investments. … 
2 CONT
2 CONT Capponi married Maddalena di Raimondo Mannelli in 1443. The Capponi and Mannelli families were closely allied during the 15th century, and the Mannellis' powerful banking connections with Catalonia and France provided a major impe
2 CONC tus for the expansion of the Capponis' business. A brother of Maddalena, Amaretto, was treasurer to the Duke of Milan in 1459, and several members of the Mannelli family were partners in the Capponi companies. Capponi had ten chil
2 CONC dren, including the famous Piero; Tommaso, who served as priore in 1494 and managed the silk company; Neri (priore in 1490 and 1508), who managed the Lyon branch for several years; and Lucrezia, who married Alamanno Salviati.
2 CONT
2 CONT Capponi died on April 23, 1487.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
