1 NOTE {geni:about_me} - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pierfrancesco_the_Elder
2 CONT
2 CONT Pierfrancesco de' Medici the Elder (1430 – 19 July 1476) was an Italian banker and diplomat, a member of the House of Medici of Florence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Florence, he was the son of Lorenzo the Elder and Ginevra Cavalcanti, and thus nephew of Cosimo de' Medici and cousin to Piero the Gouty, de facto lords of the city from 1459.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pierfrancesco was orphaned in 1440, and was raised by his uncle. He served the Republic of Florence as ambassador (to the Pope in 1458 and to Mantua in 1463) and as Priore delle Arti (1459). After Cosimo's death (1464), Pierfrance
2 CONC sco was initially a supporter of Piero, but later sided against him, being amongst the conspirators who participated in Luca Pitti's failed coup in 1466. Forgiven by Piero, he thenceforth took care of the family bank.
2 CONT
2 CONT From his marriage with Laudomia Acciaioli he had two sons: Lorenzo (1463–1503) and Giovanni (1467–1498), who were later fierce oppositors of Cosimo's line of the Medici.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pierfrancesco died in 1476. His sons were adopted by their cousin Lorenzo il Magnifico.
