1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napoleone_Orsini_(condottiero)_  ''(ENG draft)''
2 CONT
2 CONT Napoleone Orsini (c. 1420 – September 1480) was an Italian condottiero.
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of Orso Orsini of Bracciano, he fought for Pope Eugene IV against Francesco Sforza in 1443. Later, in the 1450s, he flanked Ferdinand of Aragon in the struggle between the Kingdom of Naples and the Duchy of Milan. Subseque
2 CONC ntly Orsini fought against the rival baronal families of the Colonna and the Anguillara in the Lazio.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1461, as Papal commander for Pope Pius II he defeated Sigismondo Pandolfo Malatesta, who was moving to enter the Kingdom of Naples, at Mondolfo, in the Abruzzo. The following year he was appointe commander-in-chief of the Papal
2 CONC  Army and warred against Roberto Malatesta, lord of Rimini, being wounded in the course of the campaign.
2 CONT
2 CONT Orsini did not take part in any relevant military feat thenceforth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napoleone_Orsini
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT -http://www.genmarenostrum.com/pagine-lettere/letterao/Orsini/ORSINI-BRACCIANO.htm 
2 CONT
2 CONT   F1. N.H. Napoleone (+ Roma 3-10-1480), 
2 CONT
2 CONT Signore di Bracciano (vi edificò il celebre castello), Campagnano, Trevignano, Scrofano, Bardella, Fornello, Nobile Romano e Patrizio Veneto; 7° Conte di Tagliacozzo e Albe e Barone di Cerbara dal 1456 (investito con il fratello R
2 CONC oberto il 20-3-1464, ebbe lite di successione con i Conti dell’Anguillara che gli tolsero Monticelli nel 1464), Signore di Vicovaro, Scarpa, Roccagiovine, Scanzano e Castelvecchio dal 1456; Capitano Generale di Santa Romana Chiesa
2 CONC  nel 1464 e dal 1477; vende Canino nel 1460; compra i diritti su Corbara, Carcumello, Poggio Filippo, Pagliano e Flumine e l’usufrutto sull’abbazia della Vittoria nel 1467 dalla famiglia Pagano; nel 1476, con i fratelli, abbandonò
2 CONC  i diritti a favore del Papa sui feudi e vicariati di Torre, Roccantica, Silice e Castiglione; condottiero al servizio del Re di Napoli. Possiedeva 43 feudi nel Regno di Napoli.
2 CONT
2 CONT  = Francesca Orsini, figlia di Orso Signore di Monterotondo e di Lucrezia Conti dei Signori di Valmontone (+ post 1-2-1483) (vedi/see)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT 30 August 2011 - information received:
2 CONT
2 CONT In reading about the recent wedding of Petra Ecclestone to James Stunt I learned that their wedding took place at Castello Orsini-Odescalchi in Italy. The official website for the castle is at http://www.odescalchi.it/pagine.php?i
2 CONC dx=1&amp;amp;pg=9 and it indicates that "The construction of the Castle Odescalchi begins in 1470, commissioned by Napoleon Orsini and is completed by his son Virginio Gentil in 1485." Not sure if it's the same Napolean Orsini but
2 CONC  it appears to be possible as the time frame is right.
2 CONT
2 CONT More about him: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napoleone_Orsini
2 CONT
2 CONT Potrait of a possible descendant of his, circa 1628: http://www.getty.edu/art/gettyguide/artObjectDetails?artobj=428
2 CONT
2 CONT More regarding the Orsini family: http://www.enotes.com/topic/Orsini_family  AND http://www.newadvent.org/cathen/11325b.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Just thought I'd share.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sincerely,
2 CONT
2 CONT Leigh Cagilaba
2 CONT --------
2 CONT ----------
