2 CONT Individuals (2 total)
2 CONT Tornaquinci, Marobotto di Francesco di M. Simone	frn	 circa 1441 (date is approximate) [Marobotto, son of Francesco, son of Messer Simone], ''fl.'' circa 1441
2 CONT Tornaquinci, Bernardo di Marabottino di M. Cardinale di M. Jacopo	burial [Bernardo, son of Marabottino, son of Messer Cardinale, son of Messer Jacopo Tornaquinci]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === Analyzing the Sepoltuario Database Record ===
2 CONT From Google Gemini AI
2 CONT
2 CONT This primary record from the '''Sepoltuario Campori / IATH (University of Virginia)''' database provides exact historical confirmation for the burial and inscription of this specific family branch.
2 CONT
2 CONT Here is the breakdown of what this record establishes:
2 CONT
2 CONT === 1. The Burial Location (Inscription #565) ===
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Church:''' '''Santa Croce''' in Florence (Memorial ID #170).
2 CONT * '''Inscription Text:''' ''S. Bernardi Marabottini de Tornaquincis''
2 CONT * ''Translation:'' "Tomb (''Sepulcrum'') of Bernardo [son of] Marabottino de' Tornaquinci [and his descendants]."
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Context:''' While the main branch of the Tornaquinci held their primary patronal chapel in Santa Maria Novella, this specific entry confirms that '''Bernardo di Marabottino's branch (the Marabottini)''' established their own 
2 CONC family tomb and burial rights inside '''Santa Croce'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT === 2. The Individuals Linked to the Site ===
2 CONT The database associates two distinct individuals with this family line/tomb entry:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. '''Tornaquinci, Bernardo di Marabottino di M. Cardinale di M. Jacopo'''
2 CONT * '''Role:''' The original founder/patron of the tomb inscription.
2 CONT * '''Identity:''' This is the father of '''Dianora di Bernardo Marabottini''' (mother of Tanai Nerli). His full patronymic chain traces back four generations: ''Bernardo → Marabottino → Messer Cardinale → Messer Jacopo Tornaquinci
2 CONC ''.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. '''Tornaquinci, Marobotto di Francesco di M. Simone''' (''fl.'' c. 1441)
2 CONT * '''Role:''' A downstream descendant/relative belonging to the same Marabottini collateral line who shared burial rights in the family tomb at Santa Croce.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Relationship Analysis ===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marobotto di Francesco di M. Simone''' is '''not''' Dianora's brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Here is why, based on their distinct male-line patronymic chains:
2 CONT
2 CONT === 1. Dianora's Paternal Lineage ===
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dianora's Father:''' '''Bernardo''' di Marabottino di M. Cardinale di M. Jacopo Tornaquinci.
2 CONT * '''Dianora's Grandfather:''' '''Marabottino''' di M. Cardinale.
2 CONT * '''Dianora's Great-Grandfather:''' '''Messer Cardinale''' di M. Jacopo.
2 CONT
2 CONT === 2. Marobotto's Paternal Lineage ===
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Marobotto's Father:''' '''Francesco''' di M. Simone.
2 CONT * '''Marobotto's Grandfather:''' '''Messer Simone''' Tornaquinci.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Conclusion ===
2 CONT Because Marobotto's father was '''Francesco''', whereas Dianora's father was '''Bernardo''', they cannot be full siblings.
2 CONT
2 CONT They are cousins belonging to collateral branches of the broader '''Marabottini / Tornaquinci''' house who shared rights to the same family sepulcher (Inscription #565) in Santa Croce.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Summary ===
2 CONT This record from the Virginia ''Sepoltuario'' project directly connects the '''Bernardo di Marabottino''' who fathered Dianora to a physical tomb in Santa Croce (''Inscription 565''), proving that his line held an established sepu
2 CONC lcher under the name '''Marabottini de Tornaquincis'''.
2 CONT
