2 CONT * https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/71464/pg71464-images.html PALAZZO CORSI SALVIATI (now VISCONTI ARCONATI) Via Tornabuoni. No. 20. The powerful and rich “consorteria,” or clan, of the Tornaquinci had their palaces, towers, lo
2 CONC ggie and shops, where now stands this palace.
2 CONT *[https://www.academia.edu/165589804/PORTRAITURE_AND_PATRONAGE_IN_QUATTROCENTO_FLORENCE_WITH_SPECIAL_REFERENCE_TO_THE_TORNAQUINCI_AND_THEIR_CHAPEL_in_S_Maria_Novella_vol_1_1985  (PDF) PORTRAITURE AND PATRONAGE IN QUATTROCENTO ...]
2 CONC   Studies the patronage history of the Tornaquinci consorteria, especially their palace and their chapels in S. Maria Novella. The focus is on the frescoes painted by Domenico Ghirlandaio 1485-90 and the portraits there, usually c
2 CONC alled the Tornabuoni chapel. “Bernardo di Bernardo, another nephew of the now deceased Zanobi Marabottini, also tried to preserve this line into the next generation.”  “Simone became a. Zanobi di Marabotti,no a Marabottini. These 
2 CONC men were from widely distant branches, sharing a common great-great-great grandfather.”
2 CONT * look at https://www.wandruszka-genealogie.eu/Antonio.php, Tornaquinci Tafel, where you will find the Toraquinci family tree, which includes Bernardo and Dianora.
