2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Filippa [di Bernardo di Marabottino] Tornaquinci''' (c. 1362 – c. 1430) was a Florentine noblewoman of the patrician Tornaquinci family, belonging to the cadet branch known as the Marabottini.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born around 1362 to Bernardo di Marabottino di Messer Cardinale Tornaquinci. Through her paternal line, she was the sister of Dianora di Bernardo Marabottini (wife of Francesco di Filippo dei Nerli and mother of the promin
2 CONC ent Florentine statesman Tanai Nerli).
2 CONT
2 CONT Filippa married into the influential Bardi family, wedded to Bartolomeo (Bartolo) di Messer Bindo di Messer Jacopo Bardi. As a member of the Florentine elite residing in the ''Oltrarno'' district, her marriage formed part of a bro
2 CONC ader network of marital alliances contracted by the Marabottini lineage with major patrician houses of 15th-century Florence. She lived to approximately 68 years of age, remaining active in public and tax records until at least 14
2 CONC 27, and died around 1430.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Sources
