2 CONT * Strocchia, Sharon T. “Remembering the Family: Women, Kin, and Commemorative Masses in Renaissance Florence.” Renaissance Quarterly 42, no. 4 (1989): 635–54. https://doi.org/10.2307/2862275. https://www.jstor.org/stable/2862275
2 CONT * Prajda, Katalin. ''Network and Migration in Early Renaissance Florence, 1378–1433: Friends of Friends in the Kingdom of Hungary.'' Amsterdam: Amsterdam University Press, 2018. JSTOR,  < [https://www.jstor.org/content/pdf/oa_book
2 CONC _monograph/j.ctvfp63mt PDF] > The Tornaquinci family is listed within the broader analysis of Florentine domestic intermarriages (including alliances with the Bardi and Nerli). This illustrates how patrician families maintained th
2 CONC eir local political weight in Florence while their kinsmen managed international trade networks abroad.
