2 CONT https://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/gino-capponi_res-d82ade3d-87e9-11dc-8e9d-0016357eee51_(Dizionario-Biografico)/
2 CONT
2 CONT C. married Maddalena di Raimondo Mannelli in 1443. The Capponi and Mandelli families were closely allied in the century. XV, and the powerful banking links of the Mannelli with Catalonia and France gave considerable incentive to t
2 CONC he expansion of the business of the Capons. A brother of Maddalena, Amaretto, was in 1459 treasurer of the Duke of Milan, and several members of the Mannelli family were members of the Capponi companies. C. had ten children, inclu
2 CONC ding the famous Piero, Tommaso, who was prior in 1494 and who directed the silk art company, Neri (prior in 1490 and 1508), who directed the Lyon branch for several years, and Lucrezia who married Alamanno Salviati.
2 CONT
