1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/antonio-barberini_res-2e82527b-87e7-11dc-8e9d-0016357eee51_(Dizionario-Biografico)
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT Antonio Barberini and his brother Carlo were successful Florentine grain, wool and textile merchants. Their family was originally a family of minor nobility from the Tuscan town of Barberino Val d'Elsa, who settled in Florence dur
2 CONC ing the early part of the eleventh century.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1530 Antonio participated in the defense of the Florentine Republic but after the capture of the city by Imperial troops, and the return to power of the Medici, Antonio grew weary of Medici rule and left Florence in 1537 to ove
2 CONC rsee Barberini business in Rome.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1552, Carlo's son Francesco followed his uncle to Rome and business flourished. Francesco became a very rich man and bought a number of high offices within government and the Catholic church. In 1559, his uncle Antonio was murd
2 CONC ered by forces loyal to the Medici.
2 CONT
2 CONT Francesco continued build his fortune and amass titles until his death in 1600. Ordinarily his estate would have been "fined" by the Camera Apostolica (for operating business while holding church office) but his relatives successf
2 CONC ully appealed to the head of the organization Francesco had, himself, once directed. The continuation of Barberini business fell to his nephews (the sons of his brother, also Antonio Barberini, who had died in 1571) including Maff
2 CONC eo Barberini. Thus the Barberini dynasty was founded.
