2 CONT c)         LUCCHINO Visconti (24 Aug 1346-Venice 1399).  The Chronicon of Pietro Azario names "Luchinum" as the son of "Luchinus…Vicecomes" and his second wife "Dominam Elisabetham de Flisco sororem…Domini Johannis de Flisco"[146]
2 CONC .  The Annales Mediolanenses record that "Domina Elisabet de Flisco uxor…Domini Luchini", after the death of her husband, fled Milan "cum filio suo parvulo Luchino novello" and settled in Genoa[147].  The Annales Mediolanenses rec
2 CONC ord that "Domino Luchino Novello Vicecomitis" secretly returned to Milan in 1370[148].  He became a citizen of Venice.  The testament of "dominus Luchinus Vicecomes natus quondam…domini Luchini Vicecomitis olim Mediolani…vicaris g
2 CONC eneralis, civis Venetiarum et Mediolani", dated 7 Jul 1399, requested burial "Mediolani in capella…sanctum Francischum" or, if the duke of Milan did not consent, at "Florentie ad locum sancti Francisci", bequeathed property to "do
2 CONC mine Magdalene consorti mee…filiarum mearum, tam natarum, quam nasciturarum et etiam filiorum meorum…Catherine et Magdalene filiabus meis…" and referred to the marriage contract between "Isabella filia mea cum Galeoto de Branchale
2 CONC onibus de Castro Durante"[149].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' MADDALENA, daughter of --- (-after 7 Jul 1399).  The testament of "dominus Luchinus Vicecomes natus quondam…domini Luchini Vicecomitis olim Mediolani…vicaris generalis, civis Venetiarum et Mediolani", dated 7 Jul 1399, beq
2 CONC ueathed property to "domine Magdalene consorti mee…filiarum mearum, tam natarum, quam nasciturarum et etiam filiorum meorum…Catherine et Magdalene filiabus meis…"[150].  Lucchino & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *i)          ISABELLA Visconti (-after 7 Jul 1399).  The testament of "dominus Luchinus Vicecomes natus quondam…domini Luchini Vicecomitis olim Mediolani…vicaris generalis, civis Venetiarum et Mediolani", dated 7 Jul 1399, referre
2 CONC d to the marriage contract between "Isabella filia mea cum Galeoto de Branchaleonibus de Castro Durante"[151].  Betrothed (before 7 Jul 1399) to GALEOTTO di Brancaleono, son of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *ii)         CATARINA Visconti (-after 7 Jul 1399).  The testament of "dominus Luchinus Vicecomes natus quondam…domini Luchini Vicecomitis olim Mediolani…vicaris generalis, civis Venetiarum et Mediolani", dated 7 Jul 1399, bequeat
2 CONC hed property to "…Catherine et Magdalene filiabus meis…"[152]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *iii)        MADDALENA Visconti (-after 7 Jul 1399).  The testament of "dominus Luchinus Vicecomes natus quondam…domini Luchini Vicecomitis olim Mediolani…vicaris generalis, civis Venetiarum et Mediolani", dated 7 Jul 1399, bequea
2 CONC thed property to "…Catherine et Magdalene filiabus meis…"[153]. 
