1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francesco_II_Acciaioli
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Francesco II Acciaioli''' (died 1460), called '''Franco''', was the last Duke of Athens. He was the son of Duke Antonio II Acciaioli and Maria Zorzi but had only ruled for two years (1455–1456) when the Turkish army under Turah
2 CONC anoğlu Ömer Bey arrived in Athens. The duke and his citizens hid themselves in the Acropolis and held out against the Turks until June 1458, when they were forced to surrender. Mehmed II entered Athens in August 1458, and allowed 
2 CONC Franco to retain lordship of Thebes as his vassal. Franco also reportedly became one of Mehmed's many lovers.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1460, Mehmed was informed by his Janissaries of a plot to place Franco once more in Athens. Franco was summoned to the Morea by Zaganos Pasha, one of the sultan's governors. After a long night of entertainment, Zaganos Pasha to
2 CONC ld Franco that his last hour had struck. Franco's last request was to be killed in his own tent, which was honored.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/franco-acciaiuoli_(Dizionario-Biografico)/
2 CONT
