1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Jean-François de Gondi (1584 - 21 March 1654)==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Voir [http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jean-Fran%C3%A7ois_de_Gondi '''Wikipedia...'''], [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jean_Fran%C3%A7ois_de_Gondi Jean-François de Gondi, En]
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean-François de Gondi was the first archbishop of Paris, from 1622 to 1654.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Albert de Gondi and Claude Catherine de Clermont. He was a member of the Gondi family, which had held the bishopric of Paris for nearly a century, and would continue to do so after him. Jean-François succeeded hi
2 CONC s brother Henri de Gondi. Henri had himself succeeded his uncle Pierre de Gondi (1533-1616), cardinal and commendatory abbot of the abbeys of Saint-Aubin-d'Angers, La Chaume, Sainte-Croix de Quimperlé and Buzay. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He refused his blessing to the Company of the Blessed Sacrament, even though Louis XIII wrote him a personal letter in 1631 requesting him to do so.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following his death in Paris, he was succeeded by his nephew [https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-Fran%C3%A7ois-Paul-de-Gondi-cardinal-de-Retz/6000000026981401349 '''Jean-François Paul de Gondi'''], cardinal of Retz. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Notes and references''':
2 CONT * [https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/04184a.htm Goyau, Georges. "Compagnie du Saint-Sacrement." The Catholic Encyclopedia Vol. 4.] New York: Robert Appleton Company, 1908. 23 May 2021 
2 CONT * Jean-François de Gondi, archbishop of Paris, was bought back the château, after Jean de Bueil's death (comte de Sancerre), which [https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-de-Gondi-II/6000000178399154916 '''Jean-Baptiste de Gondi, II.'''
2 CONC ] son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Baron-J%C3%A9r%C3%B4me-de-Gondi-de-Codun-II/6000000178386936860 '''Baron Jérôme de Gondi, de Codun, II'''] sold to Jean de Bueil in 1618.
