1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From "The Spinelli of Florence: Fortunes of a Renaissance Merchant Family" by Philip Jacks and William Caferro. (https://books.google.com/books?id=xr3cD7jJdLUC):
2 CONT
2 CONT "Only one of Tommaso's contemporaries left literary remains, namely, his cousin Ser Ricco di Domenico, who had served as auditor of the Ruota in the administration of Martin V and in 1444 as official notary of the Signoria during 
2 CONC the enlargement of the Palazzo Vecchio.  In his diary, begun around 1444, Ser Ricco interspersed notes on the city's history from as far back as 1282, along with news of current events."
