1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bartolomeo (Bartolo)  Bardi was a 14th-to-15th-century Florentine patrician belonging to the prominent Bardi lineage (a branch recorded in civic manuscripts as ''poi del Palagio'').
2 CONT
2 CONT His patronym was [di M. Bindo di M. Jacopo di Bartolo di M. Jacopo].  M. = messer, equivalent to Sir.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lineage & Family
2 CONT
2 CONT * Paternal Lineage: He was the son of Messer Bindo di M. Jacopo di Bartolo di M. Jacopo di Ricco Bardi. Through his direct paternal line, he was the great-great-grandson of Bartolo di M. Jacopo di Ricco Bardi (d. 1310).
2 CONT * Marriage: He married Filippa (mona) [di Bernardo di Marabottino] Tornaquinci (c. 1362 - c. 1430), daughter of Bernardo di Marabottino Tornaquinci and sister of Dianora Marabottini.
2 CONT * Children: he fathered at least two sons:
2 CONT ** Bernardo di Bartolo Bardi (who married Cecca di Doffo Spini, Gismonda di Antonio Altoviti, and Mona Nanna).
2 CONT ** Vieri di Bartolo Bardi. (Not shown as a son of Filippa.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Siblings: His recorded siblings included Andrea, Giovanni, Jacopo, and Piera Bardi.
2 CONT * Who was his mother, Lisa della Rena or Spinetta Bocchini?
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT === Generational Lineage ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Aligning the exact ancestral chain leading down to '''Bartolomeo''' (the husband of Filippa Tornaquinci) using the “Sepoltuario” database's explicit patronymic string:
2 CONT
2 CONT > '''Bartolomeo ⟶ di M. Bindo ⟶ di M. Jacopo ⟶  di Bartolo ⟶ di M. Jacopo ⟶ di Ricco ⟶ di Bardo'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 1: Ancestor 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ricco di Bardo Bardi''' (detto Lapo) Floruit: c. 1190 – c. 1230
2 CONT * Early 13th-century lineage founder who established the branch during the rise of the Florentine merchant guilds.
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 2: Great-Great-Great-Grandfather 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Messer Jacopo di Ricco di Bardo Bardi''' Floruit: c. 1220 – c. 1260
2 CONT * Married a daughter of ''messer'' Abate Mannelli.
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 3: Great-Great-Grandfather
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Bartolo di M. Jacopo di Ricco Bardi''' (d. 19 Jan 1310) https://www.geni.com/people/Bartolo-Bardi/6000000094713824821 Floruit: c. 1250 – 1310
2 CONT * Prior of Florence and merchant of the Arte della Calimala. His exact death date is documented on January 19, 1310, and husband of Tedalda Acciaiuoli (subject of the ''Dizionario Biografico'' entry)
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 4: Great-Grandfather 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Messer Jacopo di Bartolo di M. Jacopo Bardi''' Floruit: c. 1280 – c. 1340
2 CONT * Son of Bartolo and Tedalda Acciaiuoli; Knighted in the early-to-mid 14th century and active during the height of the Bardi banking operations prior to the 1345 crash.
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 5: Grandfather 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Messer Bindo di M. Jacopo di Bartolo Bardi''' Floruit: c. 1310 – c. 1370
2 CONT * Prominent patrician holding civic honors (''Messer'') in the mid-14th century following the restructuring of the Bardi company.
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 6: Father 
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Messer Bindo (or Jacopo) di M. Bindo Bardi''' Floruit: c. 1340 – c. 1395
2 CONT * Father of Bartolomeo; active during the late 14th-century political realignments in Florence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 7: Husband of Filippa
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Bartolomeo (Bartolo) di M. Bindo Bardi''' Floruit: c. 1370 – c. 1425
2 CONT * ''Husband of Filippa Tornaquinci (c. 1362–c. 1430); recorded across late 14th and early 15th-century Florentine parish and burial registers (Sepoltuario).
2 CONT ===Summary of Key Connections 
2 CONT *'''The Bardi Family Line:''' Alternates continuously between ''Jacopo'' and ''Bartolo'' due to the traditional Florentine custom of naming firstborn sons after their grandfathers.
2 CONT *'''The Tornaquinci Sibling Relationship:''' '''Filippa (mona) di Bernardo di Marabottino Tornaquinci''' (wife of Bartolomeo Bardi) is confirmed as the full biological sister of '''Dianora di Bernardo Marabottini''' (wife of Franc
2 CONC esco di Filippo Nerli and mother of Tanai Nerli).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === Branch Connection: Bartolomeo and Alessandro ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Alessandro di Sozzo de' Bardi (Count of Vernio, father of Contessina) and Bartolomeo di M. Bindo (husband of Filippa Tornaquinci) were second cousins, once removed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Both branches split directly from Messer Jacopo di Bartolo Bardi (Great-Great-Grandfather in Bartolomeo's line).
2 CONT
2 CONT Step-by-Step Relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Common Ancestor: Messer Jacopo di Bartolo Bardi.
2 CONT
2 CONT First Cousin Level: Totto di M. Jacopo (Vernio branch) was a brother to Messer Bindo di M. Jacopo (Bartolomeo's branch).
2 CONT
2 CONT Downstream Generational Shift: While Bartolomeo's line descended through Messer Bindo → Messer Bindo → Bartolomeo, the Vernio line went Totto → Messer Piero → Sozzo → Alessandro.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alessandro di Sozzo Bardi belonged to the same generation as Bartolomeo's father, making him a second cousin to Bartolomeo's father and a second cousin, once removed to Bartolomeo himself.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT * https://sepoltuario.iath.virginia.edu/individuals/9491 
