2 CONT * Prajda, Katalin. ''Network and Migration in Early Renaissance Florence, 1378–1433: Friends of Friends in the Kingdom of Hungary.'' Amsterdam: Amsterdam University Press, 2018. JSTOR,  < [https://www.jstor.org/content/pdf/oa_book
2 CONC _monograph/j.ctvfp63mt PDF] > In Chapter IV (''The Outer Circle of the Network: Friends of Business''), Prajda focuses on figures like '''Nofri di Bardo de' Bardi''', who served as a royal administrator and commercial node connect
2 CONC ing Florentine merchant interests with the court of King Sigismund in Hungary. The monograph demonstrates that while the original grand Bardi company had fallen in 1345, Bardi descendants operated as key business agents, administr
2 CONC ators, and nobility embedded in foreign courts.
