2 CONT
2 CONT Fabio Orsini (1476-29 December 1504) was an Italian condottiero and lord of Mentana. He was son of Paolo Orsini, who was murdered in 1503 by Cesare Borgia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cesare Borgia apprehended Vitellozzo Vitelli and Paolo Orsini, so Fabio fled when he saw the arrest of them. On August 23, Ludovico of Pitigliano and Fabio Orsini came with 400 horse and 500 foot soldiers. The alliance between the
2 CONC  Borgia and the Colonna saved Caesar from, and on August 24 Ludovico was yielded and Fabio dismayed.
2 CONT
2 CONT At nineteen, he became a mercenary and brave and ruthless warrior, took many battles and died of a head wound on 29 December 1503 during the battle of Garigliano
