1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicole_de_Savigny
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicole de Savigny, Baroness Fontette (department of Aube ) and Dame of Saint-Rémy,Baroness of Saint-Rémy de Luze in Champagne( France)  born in 1535 in Lorraine and died on 4 March 1590 , was a mistress of Henry II , King of Franc
2 CONC e . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of William de Savigny, Lord de Sailly, and Nicole Maretz, married very young Jean de Ville, Baron de Saint-Rémy, Lord Fontette, and gave him two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Andrew Hall, Baron de Saint-Rémy, Lord Fontette, died childless. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Elizabeth City, lady Fosse aux Loups, which enter into religion. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Young widow of 17 years when her husband died in 1552, she went to the Court and becomes 1556 the mistress of Henry II, taking advantage of a time when the king leaves his beloved favorite, Diane de Poitiers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She has a son, Henri de Saint-Rémy, born in 1557 in Paris.  His short favor with the king ends shortly after the birth of her son, when Diane de Poitiers takes his influence over Henry II.  She then retired to Fontette on his land
2 CONC , before contracting with Claude de La Baume-Montrevel, titular archbishop of Besançon , a secret marriage that the court of the Rota void. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Nicole de Savigny mentions in his will written 12 January 1590, the king made ​​him a gift for their son, Henri de Valois de Saint-Rémy, the sum of 30,000 crowns that Henry III had set him on 23 February 1577 and which it has rec
2 CONC eived 26 February 1577, although this son might not be recognized by the king. 
2 CONT
