2 CONT
2 CONT Louise, Princess of France (August 19, 1515 - September 21, 1517) - died young. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charlotte, Princess of France (October 23, 1516 - September 8, 1524) - died young. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis, Dauphin of France (February 28, 1518 - August 10, 1536) - died young. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry II, King of France (March 31, 1519 - July 10, 1559) - married Catherine de' Medici. Had issue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Madeleine, Princess of France (August 10, 1520 - July 2, 1537) - married James V of Scotland. No issue 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles of Valois, Duke of Orleans (January 22, 1522 - September 9, 1545) - Died young. Had no issue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite of France (June 5, 1523 - September 14, 1574) - married Emmanuel Philibert, Duke of Savoy in 1559. Had issue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Death and later events
2 CONT
2 CONT Claude died in 1524, when she was only twenty-four. She was initially succeeded as ruler of Brittany by her eldest son, the Dauphin François, who became Duke François III, with Claude's widower King François I as guardian. After t
2 CONC he Dauphin's untimely death in 1536, Claude's second son, Henry, Duke of Orleans, became Dauphin and Duke of Brittany. He later became King of France as Henry II.
2 CONT
2 CONT Claude's widowed husband himself remarried several years after Claude's death, to Eleanor of Habsburg, the sister of Emperor Charles V. The atmosphere at court became considerably more debauched, and there were rumours that King F
2 CONC rançois's death in 1547 was due to syphilis.
2 CONT
