1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giulia_della_Rovere
2 CONT
2 CONT Giulia della Rovere (1531, Casteldurante – 4 April 1563, Ferrara) was an Italian noblewoman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Life
2 CONT Guilia was the daughter of Francesco Maria I della Rovere, Duke of Urbino and Eleonora Gonzaga.[1] On 3 January 1549 she married Alfonso d'Este,[2] an illegitimate son of Alfonso I d'Este, Duke of Ferrara, and of Laura Dianti.[3] 
2 CONC They had:
2 CONT
2 CONT Cesare, Duke of Modena (8 October 1552 – 11 December 1628); married Virginia de' Medici[4]
2 CONT Alfonsino (14 November 1560 – 4 September 1578), married his cousin Marfisa d'Este
2 CONT Eleonora (Ferrara, 1561–Naples, 1637); married the composer, Carlo Gesualdo.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/details/G65X-RM2
