1 OCCU The marriage brought Maximilian a rich dowry & allowed him to assert his rights as Imperial overlord of Milan
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT Maximilian's third wife was '''Bianca Maria Sforza''' (1472–1510) – they were married in 1493, the marriage bringing Maximilian a rich dowry and allowing him to assert his rights as imperial overlord of Milan. The marriage was unh
2 CONC appy, and they had no children.
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bianca_Maria_Sforza '''Bianca Maria Sfroza'''] - Wikipedia - Deutsch
2 CONT * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bianca_Maria_Sforza '''Bianca Maria Sfroza'''] - Wikipedia - English (car)
2 CONT * [https://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/bianca-maria-sforza-regina-dei-romani-e-imperatrice_(Dizionario-Biografico)_ “Bianca Maria Sforza, regina dei Romani e imperatrice“] -  Treccani - Italian 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Galeazzo Maria I Sforza, duca di Milano and his second wife,  Bonne de Savoie, duchesse de Milan
2 CONT * Fiancée (unconsummated marriage) of Philibert de Savoy, 'the Hunter', betrothed at her age 21 months on 6 January 1474 (perhaps 1476).  He was her first cousin, the son of her uncle Amadeus IX of Savoy, and Yolande of France. He
2 CONC  died from tuberculosis, in Lyons, at the age of 17 and the duchy was inherited by his younger brother Charles. She was 10,; they had no children, and she returned to live in Milan under the tutelage of her uncle Ludovico Il Moro.
2 CONT * Fiancée of János (Ivaniš) Corvinus (Korvin), Graf von Hunyadi.  (Engagement announced on 31 July 1485,  marriage by proxy signed on 25 November 1487; formal marriage never took place.)
2 CONT * Wife of Maximilian I, Holy Roman Emperor (m. 1494) 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From < [https://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/bianca-maria-sforza-imperatrice/?search=Bianca%20Mar%C3%ACa%20Sforza%20imperatrice%2F treccani.it] > (google translation)
2 CONT
2 CONT Bianca Maria Sforza, Empress
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter (Milan 1472 - Innsbruck 1510) of Galeazzo Maria Sforza , she was promised in marriage, by her father and then by her uncle Ludovico il Moro, subsequently, in the changing game of alliances, to Duke Filiberto of Savoy , to
2 CONC  Albert III Duke of Bavaria , to the son of Matthias Corvinus, and finally to Ladislaus II of Bohemia and James of Scotland. Finally, in 1494, Bianca Maria married the Emperor Maximilian who promised the succession of the Duchy of
2 CONC  Milan to Moro. Childless and a stranger to the life of the German court, she only cared about maintaining good relations between her husband and her uncle Ludovico, whose children she hosted after the collapse of the family (1500
2 CONC ).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Fron < [https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bianca_Maria_Sforza Wikipedia] >, der freien Enzyklopädie
2 CONT
2 CONT Wechseln zu: Navigation, Suche
2 CONT
2 CONT Bianca Maria Sforza, Gemälde von Ambrogio de Predis, um 1493
2 CONT
2 CONT Bianca Maria Sforza auch Maria Blanca Sforza (* 5. April 1472 in Mailand; † 31. Dezember 1510 in Innsbruck) war die zweite Gemahlin des deutschen Königs Maximilian I. (1459–1519). Damit war sie ab 1494 deutsche Königin und Erzherz
2 CONC ogin von Österreich und seit 1508 Kaiserin des Heiligen Römischen Reiches.
2 CONT
2 CONT Inhaltsverzeichnis
2 CONT
2 CONT [Anzeigen]
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 1 Kindheit und Jugend
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 2 Späteres Leben
2 CONT
