2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://play.google.com/store/books/details?id=PyQtAAAAYAAJ&rdid=book-PyQtAAAAYAAJ&rdot=1
2 CONT
2 CONT ''The Santuario of the Madonna Di Vico: Pantheon of Charles Emanuel I. of Savoy'' (c. 1907) by L. Melano Rossi
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Emanuel I., Duke of Savoy, was the founder of the Santuario of the Madonna di Vico, which he named "The Temple of Peace." Born at Rivoli in 1562, he succeeded his father, Emanuel Philibert, at the age of eighteen. His moth
2 CONC er was Marguerite of Valois, sister of Henry II., King of France. It was through her that he laid claim to the crown of France when, after the death of the children of this French king, the Pope opposed the election of Henry of Na
2 CONC varre, a Huguenot. In 1585 he was married at Saragossa to a daughter of Philip II., Catherine of Austria, Infanta of Spain, through whom he later aspired to the Spanish throne. On his arrival at Saragossa he was invested with the 
2 CONC Order of the Golden Fleece and presented with the sword of Francis I. of France, taken from him by Charles V. at the battle of Pavia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Emanuel was a model of the happy husband in love with his wife. When he wrote to her he used her native language :
2 CONT
2 CONT Fece eseguire un gioiello per racchiudere il ritratto di colei che era morta d' affetto per lui, disegnando di sua mano un piccolo modello. Era una specie di medaglione chiuso, il quale aprendosi, da una parte lasciava vedere il r
2 CONC itratto della principessa con questo motto : "Morte levar non la può, Amor la impresse," e dall' altro i due C intrecciati, incoronati della corona ducale, attorniati da S., e con sotto un nodo d' amore, ed il motto :
2 CONT
2 CONT Altra tomba quaggiù non può avere Caterina Real che il cor di Carlo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Egli raccolse poi, con cura minuziosa, ogni piccolo oggetto a cui fosse legato un ricordo di lei, e tutto conservò gelosamente. Si era fatto come un museo di coserelle che gli rammentavano tanti felici momenti, e in questo vi figu
2 CONC rava sino un foglietto di carta, su cui la Duchessa aveva posato la mano, e colla penna, forse la stessa con cui il Duca attendeva a scrivere, aveva per scherzo disegnato i loro ritratti. Chi sa quanti ricordi erano legati, per Ca
2 CONC rlo Emanuele, a quel pezzetto di carta ! Egli vi scrisse sotto di suo pugno, in spagnuolo, la lingua più usata da lei : " Fatto di mano della mia signora." Poi le eorde del suo cuore, scosse dal dolore, vibrarono fortemente, e poe
2 CONC tò, ed ecco qui un saggio de' suoi versi, fatti in quella occasione.
2 CONT
2 CONT Albergo ove il mio ben stette c si piacque, Com' or mi torna in voi il mio destino ? Il sol gia si spari nel bel mattino, Tu cieco io senza luce Restiamo allo sparir del lume amato E cosi con ragione anco s' induce Il mio dolor di
2 CONC  star con te alloggiato
2 CONT
2 CONT (English translation per Google):
2 CONT
2 CONT He had a jewel made to enclose the portrait of the one who had died of affection, drawing a small model by himself. It was a kind of closed medallion which, opening up on one side, let the princess's portrait be seen with this mot
2 CONC to: "Death cannot rise, Love impresses," and on the other hand the two C's entwined, crowned with the ducal crown, surrounded by S., and with a knot of love underneath, and the motto:
2 CONT
2 CONT Another tomb down here cannot have Caterina Real that Carlo's heart.
2 CONT
2 CONT He then collected, with meticulous care, every little object to which a memory of her was tied, and all kept jealously. It was like a museum of coserelle that reminded him of so many happy moments, in it there appeared a little pi
2 CONC ece of paper, on which the Duchess had laid her hand, and with the pen, perhaps the same one with which the Duke was waiting to write, she had jokingly designed their portraits. Who knows how many memories were linked, for Carlo E
2 CONC manuele, to that piece of paper! He wrote under his hand, in Spanish, the language most used by her: "Made by the hand of my lady." Then the hordes of his heart, shaken by grief, vibrated strongly, and he poetized, and here was a 
2 CONC sage of his verses, made on that occasion.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hotel where my well-being was appreciated,
2 CONT
2 CONT How did my destiny come back to you?
2 CONT
2 CONT The sun is already blown away in the fine morning,
2 CONT
2 CONT Blind I am without your light
2 CONT
2 CONT Let us remain at the disappearance of the beloved light
2 CONT
2 CONT And so with reason it is also induced
2 CONT
2 CONT My sorrow of being lodged with you...
2 CONT
