1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Isabella of Portugal''' ( 24 October 1503 – 1 May 1539) was the daughter of Manuel I of Portugal and Maria of Aragon.  She was Holy Roman Empress and Queen of Spain, Germany, Italy, Naples and Sicily and Duchess
2 CONC  of Burgundy by her marriage to Emperor Charles V, and regent of Spain during the absences of her husband during 1529-1532, 1535-1536 and 1538-1539.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isabella_of_Portugal retrieved 18 May 2019
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Contents
2 CONT
