2 CONT Joanna "The Mad" of Aragon and Castile(1479-1555)
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor of Habsburg, also called Leonor of Castile or Eleanor of Austria was born Archduchess of Austria and Infanta of Castile, became subsequently in turn queen consort of Portugal (1518–1521) and of France, also duchess of Tour
2 CONC aine (1547–1558) as dower. Named Leonor de Austria in Spanish, Leonor(a) in Portuguese and "royne Eleonore" or Alienor in French.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses:
2 CONT 1) - Emanuel I, King of Portugal (1469-1521)
2 CONT 2) - Francois I, King of France (1494-1547)
