1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antonio_Marcello_Barberini
2 CONT
2 CONT Antonio Marcello Barberini was an Italian cardinal and younger brother of Maffeo Barberini, later Pope Urban VIII, who elevated him to cardinal in 1624. He is sometimes referred to as Antonio the Elder to distinguish him from his 
2 CONC nephew Antonio Barberini.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Florence into the Barberini family, he was a member of the Order of Capuchins.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was appointed Bishop of Senigallia between 1625 and 1628. Later he was appointed Grand Inquisitor of the Roman Inquisition between 1629 and 1633, Librarian of the Holy Roman Church between 1633 and 1646 and Grand penitentiary b
2 CONC etween 1633 and 1646. He served as the Camerlengo of the Sacred College of Cardinals twice.
2 CONT
2 CONT He participated in the papal conclave of 1644 which elected his brother's successor, Pope Innocent X. Innocent X was hostile to the Barberini family and later forced Antonio Barberini's nephews, Francesco Barberini (Senior), Anton
2 CONC io Barberini (Antonio the Younger) and Prince Taddeo Barberini, into exile.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barberini died at Rome, at the age of 77.
2 CONT
