2 CONT 1.         PETRONILLA Tocco (-[22 Jun 1409/27 Sep 1410]).  After her first husband's death, she was compensated by property near the hot baths of Aedepsos on the island of Eubœa.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly ([1372]) NICOLÒ dalle Carceri Lord of Eubœa Duke of Naxos and the Archipelago, son of GIOVANNI dalle Carceri Lord of Eubœa & his wife Fiorenza Sanudo Dss of Naxos and the Archipelago (-murdered Naxos 1383).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly ([1383]) as his first wife, NICOLA Vernier, son of --- Doge of Venice & his wife --- (-before 30 Sep 1422).  Venetian bailly of Negroponte 1408.  
