0 @N6000000002322286338@ NOTE After his cousin Salvestro exiled in 1381, the memory of Salvestro was still
1 CONT alive in 1393, when the popolo magro ("lean people") once again thought it
1 CONT possible to take over the signoria (government). The mob hastened to seek out
1 CONT the cousin of Salvestro, Vieri, who was, however, able to fade away without
1 CONT losing face. With Vieri, this branch of the Medici (Chiarissimo II) was to
1 CONT disappear definitively from history.
